    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSpacious Two Bedroom Second floor apartment c. 70.7 sqm in the heart of the town centre with secure carparking.\n\nThe apartment is overlooking New Street in a private development of apartments and townhouses over shop units, which include the award winning Torc Café and Food hall. \n\nIt features a large kitchen / living area, with built in units and appliances. There are two double sized bedrooms. The bath was removed in the bathroom and replaced with a large shower unit and is semi tiled. \n\nThere are two large storage cupboards providing substantial storage space.\n\nThe apartment is partially furnished and includes all appliances and comes with vacant possession. \n\nIt is an ideal small home with remote working possibilities with high speed fibre and cable gigabit broadband available.\n\n\nServices\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Electric storage heating \n• Cablecom Gigabit broadband available\n• Refuse bins for scheme\n\n\nThe Development:\nElectric security gates provide access from New street to the private carpark behind the scheme. There is elevator access to the second floor.\n \nThe service charge for 2026 is 1828.64 with a 200 discount for prompt payment. The service charge covers block insurance, refuse bins, security gates and common areas maintenance.\n\n\nLocation:\nSituated in the heart of the town centre, just off the Market Square, the apartment is convenient to all shops and services.\nLongford Train & Bus Station, with 10 daily weekday train departures to Dublin Connolly, is just 3 minutes walk from the apartment block. \n\nThe Market Square also marks the start of the Royal Canal Walkway and Cycle path that runs along the canal to Clondra Village.\n\n\nEircode: N39 DR98 \nGPS: 53.7260, -7.7977"
      },
